through the hours of meetings the dozens and dozens of conversations we've had in person plus phone calls emails texts and ultimately feel that this project has dramatically improved by taking the feedback that we've heard from the neighbors and us taking action and that's something we're really really proud of we ultimately hope that this project will raise the bar for all data centers in Cheyenne and it is a step in the right direction for better community city and industry partnerships we know we have a lot more work to do and we are excited to meaningfully continue to engage and meet with residents and stakeholders in Orchard Valley and South Cheyenne to ensure that this project is a win for everybody and

that they see their feedback continue to become action we've also received a couple questions on backup power and I wanted to address those tonight um the question question one how are you approaching the technology and cost issues related to backup power what alternatives have you evaluated can you use batteries or gas turbines uh the answer to that from TCC is that we are constantly evaluating technological advances and changes in backup power and how our sites can be better um one that we are specifically looking as a technology like batteries on site instead of backup diesel generation um but we haven't made a decision yet on this project as is usually client driven um but just want to clarify we do not use gas turbines at all

um if you decide to use generators um how are they operated for testing and what's the maximum duration they can operate so each diesel engine um or the collective group um is allowed to operate for a maximum of 35 hours per year that's about 5 minutes per day um but gens are not tested daily and that we would make the effort to coincide that testing with other emergency services like amber tornadoes things like that storm warnings um to try to limit that impact um maximum duration again um it would depend on the situation so if it's an actual utility outage obviously there's fuel um and how long the outage would last but again going back to the previously mentioned 35 hours um

will uh TCC you Tremolo Crow use tier 4 generators that's an emission um kind of cap that reduces emissions of each generator by 90% and the answer to that is that is our standard we don't use any other types of generators other than that if we use them um and then lastly um all of our generators if they're installed would be on the south side so away from the residences um we just wanted to thank you again for the opportunity to work on this project we're incredibly excited uh about the opportunity to grow in Cheyenne to be a great partner and sincerely hope that we get the chance to do so um our team is available for any questions throughout the conversation this evening thank

